# The mix/master pipeline needs no secrets. Generation (`producer generate`,
# `producer song-from-vocal`) reads these from the environment:
#
#   MIXMAX_GEN_BUDGET_USD=5.0   most a generation ledger may reach, in dollars.
#                               A call that would pass it is refused before it
#                               is made. Default 5.0.
#   MIXMAX_FAKE_BEAT=           a beat, or a folder of beats, for the `fake`
#                               backend to hand back instead of test fixtures.
#
# The studio web app (web/) needs secrets once hosted. They live in web/.env.local,
# which `vercel env pull` writes; `producer sync` reads the blob credentials
# from there. See web/README.md.
#
#   MIXMAX_PASSCODE=        shared passcode for the studio (required when deployed)
#   BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=  private Vercel Blob store
#
# Optional, for running everything on one machine against a chosen folder:
#   MIXMAX_DATA_DIR=        local store folder (default web/.data)
